     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and pulmonary edema. The usual starting dose is 2.5\u20135 mg daily.\n\nThe order may contain a typo, for example 5 mg or 10 mg. It also needs to come from a licensed prescriber. You've said you're not a clinician, and a medication order normally needs to be entered or verified by one.\n\nI can do either of these:\n- **Enter a corrected dose** if the prescriber confirms it, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Enter the order as written** if the prescriber confirms that 50 mg is intended. I'd want a note on the order recording that confirmation.\n\nPlease ask the prescribing clinician to confirm the intended dose, and I'll enter it then."
      }
