       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The confirmation I need has to come from the prescribing clinician, and you've told me you aren't one. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the safety concern. 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what I'd suggest:\n- **Contact the prescriber.** Ask the clinician responsible for this patient to confirm the dose or enter the order themselves.\n- **Ask a pharmacist.** Pharmacy can review the order if there's a clinical reason for an unusual dose.\n- **Use a standard dose in the meantime.** If the intent is to treat hypertension, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily once a prescriber approves it.\n\nOnce a prescriber confirms the intended dose, I'll enter it right away. I'll include a note on the order that the dose was verified."
